//? Title: Johnson fast style:explicit tensor training and generator-only prediction
//? Subtitle: Tensor computations, explicit checks and reproducible local figures
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Train a complete compact Johnson transformation network using genuine frozen ImageNet VGG16 content/style features and quadratic TV. Explain exact reflection,cropped residuals and learned stride phase,show all36 Adam updates with paired BN checkpoint selection,and restore a separate generator-only predictor. Original CIFAR contents,Kandinsky painting,independent Keras gradients and all held-out outputs keep the short fit reproducible.
)
\toc

Source example: `examples/cpp/source/nn/1_convolutional_neural_networks/1.8_other_vision_tasks/johnson_fast_style.cpp`.

> The method

The transformation network learns weights;the VGG16 feature extractor stays fixed. Every learnable tensor and moving BN statistic is explicit,and the report owns the optimizer,all minibatches,validation and paired checkpoint. Deployment consumes only observed RGB. Content/style targets and training objectives are confined to the demonstrated fit and evaluation.

The editable concept diagram is `diagrams/johnson_fast_style_concept.tikz`. Regeneration uses
LaTeX with PGF/TikZ and standalone, plus dvisvgm; exports use the saved SVG.

```{bash, results="output", file="figures/johnson_fast_style_concept.svg"}
set -eu
mkdir -p build
latex -interaction=batchmode -halt-on-error -output-directory=build diagrams/johnson_fast_style_concept.tikz > build/johnson_fast_style_concept.compile.log 2>&1
dvisvgm --no-fonts --bbox=10 --output=build/johnson_fast_style_concept.svg build/johnson_fast_style_concept.dvi > build/johnson_fast_style_concept.render.log 2>&1
printf 'Rendered local concept diagram.\n'
```
