> Learned upsampling has an explicit stride phase

Torch k3/s2/p1 down-convolution pads one zero sample on each side,then uses
VALID stride2. Its corresponding learned transpose uses a VALID2H+1 by2W+1
output and crops from coordinate1 to2H/2W. This matches adjustment1 and
preserves the source phase. A generic SAME stride2 can align odd padding
differently. The transpose initializer uses true fan-in9*Cin,not9*Cout.
```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/johnson_fast_style_stride.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>

#include <print>
int main() {
  namespace n = dm::nn;
  namespace m = n::models;
  n::ParameterStore p(17);
  const auto x = n::tensor({1., 0., 0., 0., 0., 0.}, {1, 2, 3, 1}).requires_grad_();
  {
    n::NoGradGuard guard;
    m::JohnsonUp(p, "up", x, 1);
    p.set("up/W", n::arange(1, 10).reshape({3, 3, 1, 1}));
    p.set("up/b", n::zeros({1}));
  }
  const auto y = m::JohnsonUp(p, "up", x, 1), gradient = n::grad(n::sum(y), {x})[0];
  std::print("2x3 observed impulse ->4x6 learned transpose;input adjoint:{}\n", gradient);
  auto a = n::plot_tensor_map(n::reverse(y.reshape({4, 6}), {0}), 0, 9),
       b = n::plot_tensor_map(n::reverse(gradient.reshape({2, 3}), {0}), 0, 45);
  a.title("Actual cropped transpose impulse")
      .x_label("output column")
      .y_label("output row0 at bottom");
  b.title("Every observed-pixel adjoint")
      .x_label("input column")
      .y_label("input row0 at bottom");
  auto layout = dm::graphics::RLayout::create(1, 2);
  layout.add(a).add(b).size(1100, 500).fit_panels().save_svg(
      "build/johnson_fast_style_stride.svg");
}
```
