// result_end
\caption(Thirty-six explicit Adam updates with separate learned/BN stores. Every validation component uses its fixed initial denominator;their sum equals validation total.)
\alttext(Thirty-six explicit Adam updates with separate learned/BN stores. Every validation component uses its fixed initial denominator;their sum equals validation total.)


\image(figures/johnson_fast_style_evaluation.svg)
\caption(All eight held-out contents compare restored versus initial frozen perceptual objectives. Distinct content inputs produce measured output differences;this check does not establish semantic fidelity or subjective style quality.)
\alttext(Held-out perceptual objective reduction and measured content-dependent generator outputs.)

\image(figures/johnson_fast_style_predictions.png)
\caption(All eight actual held-out contents,two tiles per row. Each tile is observed content,fixed genuine Kandinsky painting,and one-pass restored generator RGB. No VGG,style target or optimization occurs in the prediction call.)
\alttext(Original held-out CIFAR contents,genuine painting and actual generator-only stylized outputs.)

The selected epoch3 lowers held-out combined objective from12.357131 to
1.783372. Its fixed-scale content/style/TV contributions are
.679889/.912451/.191033. The actual outputs remain dominated by bright
colored texture with weak visual content preservation. The measured
.139763 difference across contents proves input sensitivity,but does not
establish recognizable objects or attractive style quality.

Lower frozen-feature objective measures this stated perceptual criterion;
it is not a subjective quality score or a guarantee that objects remain
recognizable. This64px compact three-epoch fit retains the original mechanism
without reproducing the paper’s dataset,training schedule,large-image quality
or real-time performance claim. The measured latency belongs to this local
CPU and input size only.

> Conclusion

Exact geometry/adjoint fixtures and independent full-width Keras feature gradients establish the mechanisms. Thirty-six visible tensor Adam updates and paired learned/BN restoration connect them to genuine source images. Separate input-only immutable prediction and all held-out previews keep the resulting fast-style claim bounded to this short CPU experiment.

> References

- [Johnson,Alahi and Fei-Fei,Perceptual Losses for Real-Time Style Transfer and Super-Resolution](https://arxiv.org/abs/1603.08155).
- [Original architecture supplementary material](https://cs.stanford.edu/people/jcjohns/papers/eccv16/JohnsonECCV16Supplementary.pdf).
- [Official Keras VGG16 implementation and pretrained weight URLs](https://github.com/keras-team/keras/blob/master/keras/src/applications/vgg16.py).
- [TensorFlow tutorial,original Kandinsky painting and image provenance](https://www.tensorflow.org/tutorials/generative/style_transfer).
